WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:01.270 align:start position:0%
 
you know one of the things i've said  before and that i continue to say  many things i continue to say one is we  can have  political disagreements with our leaders  as we will inevitably  uh have while recognizing that some  leaders  are normal and others are not  and joe biden despite not doing nearly  everything i want him to do  has brought back a degree of respect to  the united states globally  that donald trump only ever dreamed of  and this has become  so clear during the recent g7  and nato summit and joe biden's  various meetings with world leaders  remember that under donald trump  world leaders were regularly visibly  annoyed with trump  endlessly frustrated with trump trump  was increasingly just not a part of  important conversations that world  leaders  were having the reporting from the g7  and nato is stunning how quickly  respect has been restored to the office  now that doesn't mean biden's a hero  i've said so many times let's not deify  politicians they're just people and  they're flawed people  they're really just like you and me it  doesn't mean  biden is a hero it's just a reminder of  how disastrous the four years  under donald trump were now first of all  statistically  before we get to the sort of anecdotal  stuff pew research center released a  report last week documenting  the huge improvement to the united  states stature  globally after the inauguration of joe  biden  and the portion of world citizens from  12 different countries with confidence  in the united states  in the u.s president went from 17  percent when trump left office  now to 75 these these are just stunning  numbers  this is basically a quadrupling  of the confidence in the american  president  in these early months of joe biden's  presidency compared to when donald trump  left office  the portion of citizens in these 12  countries with a favorable view of the  united states  has nearly doubled from 34 to 62 percent  already  so statistically when people like you  know the three people from the my pillow  rally say the us  is now uh you know the the we should be  ashamed now  the u.s is embarrassed globally no no no  no we we have the data pew research  center studies these  this noam chomsky referred to it a  couple weeks ago when we interviewed him  the favorable view of the us has nearly  doubled around the world under trump but  then anecdotally from the g7 and nato  politico describes it as quote overall  the g7 has delivered a significant win  for biden  while the leaders were panned for not  doing enough to vaccinate the world  and frequently fell short of consensus  on the toughest issues  they're definitely moving in the same  direction and other leaders  fell over themselves to welcome biden to  their table  when french president macron was asked  about whether the u s is back  as a global leader macron said  definitely  and later said it's great to have a u.s  president  part of the club and very willing to  cooperate  german chancellor angela merkel said to  reporters at the summit  quote being able to meet joe biden is  obviously important  because he stands for the commitment to  multilateralism  which we were missing in recent years  that's a direct shot at trump  even british prime minister boris  johnson who quite frankly  politically is an adversary of biden as  a right winger  boris johnson said he was quote  absolutely thrilled to see biden  and that speaking to biden was quote a  brush breath of fresh air  heather conley who served as a deputy  assistant secretary of state  to bush cheney's administration said to  politico quote there is no longer a  feeling of complete complete dread  before a nato or g7 summit  or fearing that the meetings would upend  u.s policy  a washington post report added biden was  greeted with delight by g7 leaders  relieved that trump's tantrums  will be replaced by biden's backslapping  so let me say it again  we do not worship politicians on this  show biden is a very flawed politician  and at the end of the day he's just a  person but to deny the clear difference  here is to ignore reality now  obviously and predictably people on the  right are saying  we now are globally embarrassed that's  not backed up by the data but what is  really sad is to see even people on the  left  who see biden not just as not  progressive enough  but who want to go further and they want  to pretend that we don't have a night  and day difference from what we had  under trump guys  it's okay to recognize and still to say  biden hasn't done enough biden's not  progressive enough  biden may not achieve the things we want  him to that's fine  it's okay to say trump was a reality tv  freak show  and biden is a respectful educated  diplomat and that's a really good thing  but we still hold biden accountable on  policy it's okay to do that  but the leftists who react to this by  saying  of course merkel and boris johnson like  biden they're all the same center-right  neo-liberal or whatever um  biden's policy platform  is not that of merkel it is not that of  johnson will he achieve everything he  said he was going to no of course not  and we'll hold them accountable won't be  critical  but we really participate  in a sort of collective gaslighting if  we and by we i mean others i'm not doing  this if we pretend  that there's no night and day difference  between what trump was  and what president biden is today uh you  know the the thing trump could never buy  no matter how much he spent and no  matter how much money he had  was class and professionalism and  maturity  and uh uh tact and diplomacy and  that doesn't make biden a progressive  hero  by its very by merely being that way  um but it changes dramatically the  standing of the united states  around the world and that's a really  important thing

